msgid "\"fetch: {}\""
msgstr "\"fetch: {}\""

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:378
msgid ""
"`reject_string(message)` rejects with a real JavaScript `Error`: consumers "
"can use `error instanceof Error`, `error.message`, and `error.stack`. Use "
"`reject(value)` only when the API intentionally rejects with a non-Error "
"value, or `reject_with(...)` when the Error needs structured fields built on "
"the main thread."
msgstr ""
"`reject_string(message)` menolak dengan JavaScript `Error` nyata: konsumen "
"dapat menggunakan `error instanceof Error`, `error.message`, dan "
"`error.stack`. Gunakan `reject(value)` hanya ketika API sengaja menolak "
"dengan nilai non-Error, atau `reject_with(...)` ketika Error membutuhkan "
"bidang terstruktur yang dibangun di thread utama."

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:384
msgid "Sync handle-based class"
msgstr "Class berbasis handle yang sinkron"

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:386
msgid ""
"Use a `handle` descriptor for synchronous resource-style APIs. The native "
"function receives or returns the raw resource pointer as `i64`, while "
"TypeScript callers see only the opaque handle object."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan deskriptor `handle` untuk API bergaya resource yang sinkron. Fungsi "
"native menerima atau mengembalikan pointer resource mentah sebagai `i64`, "
"sementara pemanggil TypeScript hanya melihat objek handle yang opaque."

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:406
msgid "Event listeners (`.on(event, cb)`)"
msgstr "Event listener (`.on(event, cb)`)"

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:415
msgid "// closure pointers, kept alive by the GC scanner below"
msgstr "// penunjuk penutupan, disimpan hidup oleh GC scanner di bawah"

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:458
msgid ""
"The GC scanner is **load-bearing**: without it, a malloc-triggered GC "
"between `.on(cb)` and `.emit()` will sweep the closure and the next emit "
"calls freed memory. Always register a scanner if your handles store closure "
"pointers."
msgstr ""
"Scanner GC bersifat **load-bearing**: tanpanya, GC yang dipicu malloc antara "
"`.on(cb)` dan `.emit()` akan menyapu closure dan emit berikutnya akan "
"memanggil memori yang sudah dibebaskan. Selalu daftarkan scanner jika handle "
"Anda menyimpan pointer closure."

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:463
msgid "When to extend the perry-ffi surface"
msgstr "Kapan memperluas permukaan perry-ffi"

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:465
msgid ""
"If your binding genuinely needs something perry-ffi doesn't expose, file an "
"issue against [`PerryTS/perry`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues) "
"describing:"
msgstr ""
"Jika binding Anda benar-benar membutuhkan sesuatu yang tidak diekspos perry-"
"ffi, ajukan issue di [`PerryTS/perry`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/"
"issues) yang menjelaskan:"

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:469
msgid "the binding you're writing,"
msgstr "binding yang Anda tulis,"

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:470
msgid "the perry-runtime function/type you'd otherwise reach into,"
msgstr "fungsi/tipe perry-runtime yang sebaliknya akan Anda gunakan,"

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:471
msgid "why a higher-level perry-ffi entry would generalize."
msgstr "mengapa entri perry-ffi tingkat lebih tinggi akan menggeneralisasi."

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:473
msgid ""
"The bar for adding to perry-ffi is high — every helper is a forever "
"commitment — but real wrappers driving real needs is exactly the right "
"input. The recent additions (BigInt + Buffer in v0.5.556, JSON-stringify + "
"event-pump in v0.5.567 followups) all came from specific wrappers needing "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Standar untuk menambahkan ke perry-ffi tinggi — setiap helper adalah "
"komitmen selamanya — tetapi wrapper nyata yang mendorong kebutuhan nyata "
"adalah input yang tepat. Penambahan terbaru (BigInt + Buffer di v0.5.556, "
"JSON-stringify + event-pump di followup v0.5.567) semuanya berasal dari "
"wrapper spesifik yang membutuhkannya."

#: src/native-libraries/authoring-guide.md:479
msgid ""
"Don't reach into `perry_runtime::*` directly to \"unblock\" your wrapper "
"today — it'll break the next time those internals change."
msgstr ""
"Jangan langsung mengakses `perry_runtime::*` untuk \"membuka blokir\" "
"wrapper Anda hari ini — itu akan rusak saat internal tersebut berubah "
"berikutnya."

