#: src/container/containers.md:1
msgid "Single-Container Lifecycle (`perry/container`)"
msgstr "Siklus Hidup Single-Container (`perry/container`)"

#: src/container/containers.md:3
msgid ""
"`perry/container` exposes the OCI primitives that operate on **one container "
"at a time**: create, start, run, stop, remove, exec, logs, inspect, plus "
"image management. For multi-service stacks, see [`perry/compose`](./"
"compose.md) — but you can mix the two modules in the same program (a long-"
"running compose stack plus one-off `run()` helpers against it is a normal "
"pattern)."
msgstr ""
"`perry/container` mengekspos primitif OCI yang beroperasi pada **satu "
"container sekaligus**: create, start, run, stop, remove, exec, logs, "
"inspect, ditambah manajemen image. Untuk stack multi-layanan, lihat [`perry/"
"compose`](./compose.md) — tetapi Anda dapat mencampur kedua modul dalam "
"program yang sama (stack compose yang berjalan lama ditambah helper `run()` "
"sekali pakai terhadapnya adalah pola yang umum)."

#: src/container/containers.md:10
msgid ""
"Every async function returns a `Promise`. The runtime backend (docker, "
"podman, apple/container, …) is auto-detected on first use; see [Overview](./"
"overview.md#backend-auto-detection) for the probe order and override knobs."
msgstr ""
"Setiap fungsi async mengembalikan `Promise`. Backend runtime (docker, "
"podman, apple/container, …) dideteksi otomatis saat pertama digunakan; lihat "
"[Ikhtisar](./overview.md#backend-auto-detection) untuk urutan probe dan opsi "
"override."

#: src/container/containers.md:15
msgid "Running a container"
msgstr "Menjalankan container"

#: src/container/containers.md:17
msgid "`run()` creates and starts a container in one shot, returning a handle:"
msgstr ""
"`run()` membuat dan memulai container dalam satu langkah, mengembalikan "
"sebuah handle:"

#: src/container/containers.md:19
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { run, remove } from \"perry/container\";\n"
"\n"
"async function runAlpine(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const handle = await run({\n"
"        image: \"alpine:3.19\",\n"
"        cmd: [\"echo\", \"hello from perry\"],\n"
"        rm: false,\n"
"        // Production-friendly defaults: drop every Linux capability and\n"
"        // run as a non-root user. Add `cap_add` only for the specific\n"
"        // capabilities a workload actually needs.\n"
"        user: \"nobody\",\n"
"        cap_drop: [\"ALL\"],\n"
"    });\n"
"    console.log(`container handle: ${String(handle)}`);\n"
"\n"
"    // `force: true` removes the container even if still running (the\n"
"    // FFI calls `docker rm -f` / `podman rm -f`).\n"
"    await remove(handle as unknown as string, true);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { run, remove } from \"perry/container\";\n"
"\n"
"async function runAlpine(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const handle = await run({\n"
"        image: \"alpine:3.19\",\n"
"        cmd: [\"echo\", \"hello from perry\"],\n"
"        rm: false,\n"
"        // Production-friendly defaults: drop every Linux capability and\n"
"        // run as a non-root user. Add `cap_add` only for the specific\n"
"        // capabilities a workload actually needs.\n"
"        user: \"nobody\",\n"
"        cap_drop: [\"ALL\"],\n"
"    });\n"
"    console.log(`container handle: ${String(handle)}`);\n"
"\n"
"    // `force: true` removes the container even if still running (the\n"
"    // FFI calls `docker rm -f` / `podman rm -f`).\n"
"    await remove(handle as unknown as string, true);\n"
"}\n"
"```"

