msgstr "Pekerjaan | select(.status==\"queued\") | (label)|join(\",\"))'"

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:48
msgid ""
"Demand outran drain, the queue grew without bound, and the oldest entries — "
"the `main` runs, which are exactly the ones that gate nothing and therefore "
"nobody is watching — aged out."
msgstr ""
"Permintaan overran pembuangan, antrian tumbuh tanpa batas, dan entri tertua  "
"`main` berjalan, yang persis orang-orang yang gerbang apa-apa dan oleh "
"karena itu tidak ada yang menonton  tua keluar."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:52
msgid "What this is NOT"
msgstr "Apa ini bukan"

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:54
msgid ""
"**It is not the concurrency bug, and it is not macOS runner availability.** "
"Both were the obvious reading, and both are wrong. Getting this right "
"matters, because each wrong reading has a \"fix\" that would make things "
"worse."
msgstr ""
"**Ini bukan bug paralel, dan itu bukan ketersediaan pelari macOS.** Keduanya "
"adalah pembacaan yang jelas, dan keduanya salah. Mendapatkan ini benar "
"penting, karena setiap pembacaan yang salah memiliki \"perbaikan\" yang akan "
"membuat keadaan lebih buruk."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:58
msgid ""
"**Not the concurrency block — _as it stood in #7856_.** `gc-ratchet.yml`'s "
"`concurrency:` comment records two prior attempts (#7205): a shared group "
"with unconditional `cancel-in-progress` cancelled three consecutive `main` "
"runs, and scoping `cancel-in-progress` to pull requests did not fix it "
"either, because GitHub allows at most one _pending_ run per group. Keying "
"the group on `github.sha` for push events **did** fix cancellation. The "
"failure mode simply moved: runs stopped cancelling each other and started "
"queueing forever instead."
msgstr ""
"**Bukan blok paralel  _seperti yang ada di #7856_.** `gc-ratchet.yml`'s "
"`concurrency:` komentar mencatat dua upaya sebelumnya (#7205): kelompok "
"bersama dengan `cancel-in-progress` tanpa syarat dibatalkan tiga `main` "
"berturut-turut menjalankan, dan scoping `cancel-in-progress` untuk menarik "
"permintaan tidak memperbaikinya baik, karena GitHub memungkinkan paling satu "
"_pending_ menjalankan per kelompok. Mengunci kelompok pada `github.sha` "
"untuk acara push **benar** Perbaiki pembatalan. Mode kegagalan hanya "
"bergerak: berjalan berhenti membatalkan satu sama lain dan mulai antrian "
"selamanya sebagai gantinya."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:66
msgid ""
"**⚠️ SUPERSEDED BY #7966 — this paragraph used to end \"Those blocks are "
"correct. Do not 'fix' them again.\" That sentence was true when written and "
"false three days later, and it is exactly the sentence that would send the "
"next reader past the real bug.**"
msgstr ""
"**️ DISUPSI BY #7966  paragraf ini digunakan untuk mengakhiri \"Blok itu "
"benar. Jangan 'memperbaiki' lagi\". Kalimat itu benar ketika ditulis dan "
"salah tiga hari kemudian, dan kalimat itu persis yang akan membuat pembaca "
"berikutnya melupakan bug yang sebenarnya.**"

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:71
msgid ""
"The `github.sha` arm is guarded on `github.event_name == 'push'`. #7856 — "
"the change this very document describes — moved the main-line arm from "
"`push: branches: [main]` to `schedule:`. The guard stopped matching, the "
"expression fell through to `github.ref` (constant `refs/heads/main`), and "
"**\\#7205 came straight back on the arm \\#7856 created.** Measured "
"2026-08-12, identically on all ten gates: oldest run `queued` holding the "
"group, the next two `cancelled` with `jobs: 0`, newest `pending`. `gate-"
"freshness` itself was cancelled the same way."
msgstr ""
"Lengan `github.sha` dijaga pada `github.event_name == 'push'`. # 7856  "
"perubahan yang dijelaskan dalam dokumen ini  memindahkan lengan garis utama "
"dari `push: branches: [main]` ke `schedule:`. Penjaga berhenti cocok, "
"ungkapan jatuh melalui ke `github.ref` (konstan `refs/heads/main`), dan "
"**\\#7205 datang langsung kembali pada lengan \\#7856 dibuat.** Diukur "
"2026-08-12, identik pada semua sepuluh gerbang: tertua menjalankan `queued` "
"memegang kelompok, dua berikutnya `cancelled` dengan `jobs: 0`, terbaru "
"`pending`. `gate-freshness` sendiri dibatalkan dengan cara yang sama."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:79
msgid ""
"Groups are now keyed on `github.run_id` for every non-pull-request event, "
"which is the only context value unconditionally distinct across scheduled "
"runs. `scripts/gc_gate_wiring_check.py` (in the required `lint` context) now "
"rejects a `schedule:` workflow whose concurrency group lacks "
"`github.run_id`, so this cannot relapse a fourth time silently."
msgstr ""
"Kelompok sekarang diketik pada `github.run_id` untuk setiap acara non-pull-"
"request, yang merupakan satu-satunya nilai konteks yang berbeda tanpa syarat "
"di seluruh jadwal. `scripts/gc_gate_wiring_check.py` (dalam konteks `lint` "
"yang diperlukan) sekarang menolak alur kerja `schedule:` yang kelompok "
"paralelnya tidak memiliki `github.run_id`, sehingga ini tidak dapat kambuh "
"untuk keempat kalinya secara diam-diam."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:85
msgid ""
"**The lesson is about the sentence, not the YAML.** \"Do not fix this "
"again\" is a claim about the future, and a scheduling change three days "
"later invalidated it. A repaired invariant should be written down as an "
"_executable check_, not as an instruction to the next human to stop looking."
msgstr ""
"**Pelajaran ini tentang kalimat, bukan YAML.** \"Jangan perbaiki ini lagi\" "
"adalah klaim tentang masa depan, dan perubahan jadwal tiga hari kemudian "
"membatalkannya. Invarian yang diperbaiki harus ditulis sebagai _check yang "
"dapat dilaksanakan_, bukan sebagai instruksi kepada manusia berikutnya untuk "
"berhenti mencari."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:90
msgid ""
"**Not macOS capacity.** This was the natural inference — the gates that went "
"dark are the macOS ones — but the job-level numbers refute it. At the moment "
"of measurement the queue held **45 `ubuntu-latest` jobs against 14 "
"`macos-14` jobs**, and `zizmor` (`ubuntu-latest`) was queued in the very "
"same second as `gc-ratchet` (`macos-14`). Ubuntu was starved harder in "
"absolute terms."
msgstr ""
"**Tidak kapasitas macOS.** Ini adalah kesimpulan alami  gerbang yang gelap "
"adalah macOS  tapi angka tingkat pekerjaan menyangkalnya. Pada saat "
"pengukuran antrian diadakan **45 pekerjaan `ubuntu-latest` terhadap 14 "
"pekerjaan `macos-14`**, dan `zizmor` (`ubuntu-latest`) ditempatkan di "
"antrian pada detik yang sama dengan `gc-ratchet` (`macos-14`). Ubuntu "
"kelaparan lebih keras dalam hal absolut."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:96
msgid ""
"Two specific claims in #7856 do not survive checking, and are recorded here "
"so the next person does not re-derive them:"
msgstr ""
"Dua klaim spesifik di #7856 tidak bertahan dari pemeriksaan, dan dicatat di "
"sini sehingga orang berikutnya tidak menyimpulkan kembali:"

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:99
msgid ""
"**`gc-root-dominance` does not run on `ubuntu-latest`.** It runs `macos-14`, "
"in two jobs. Its healthy-looking run count was pull-request runs, which "
"drain because they supersede each other; its `main` arm was queued like all "
"the others. The ubuntu-vs-macOS contrast that localised the problem to macOS "
"was comparing a PR arm against a `main` arm, not Linux against Darwin."
msgstr ""
"**`gc-root-dominance` tidak berjalan pada `ubuntu-latest`.** Ini menjalankan "
"`macos-14`, dalam dua pekerjaan. Jumlah run yang terlihat sehat adalah run "
"pull-request, yang menguras karena saling menggantikan; lengan `main`nya "
"berbaris seperti yang lainnya. Kontras ubuntu-vs-macOS yang menglokalkan "
"masalah ke macOS adalah membandingkan lengan PR dengan lengan `main`, bukan "
"Linux melawan Darwin."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:104
msgid ""
"**Moving `gc-ratchet` to Linux is not available as a remedy.** Its baseline "
"is captured under the `darwin-arm64` platform key and the checker _refuses_ "
"a platform mismatch rather than comparing numbers that are not comparable. "
"Moving it would turn the gate red, not relieve it. `tls-budget`'s macOS arm "
"is likewise irreducible: `_tlv_get_addr` is a Mach-O artefact and the "
"measurement does not exist elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"**Memindahkan `gc-ratchet` ke Linux tidak tersedia sebagai solusi.** Garis "
"dasarnya ditangkap di bawah kunci platform `darwin-arm64` dan checker "
"_menolak_ ketidakcocokan platform daripada membandingkan angka yang tidak "
"dapat dibandingkan. Memindahkannya akan membuat gerbang menjadi merah, bukan "
"meringankannya. `tls-budget` macOS lengan juga tidak dapat direduksi: "
"`_tlv_get_addr` adalah artefak Mach-O dan pengukuran tidak ada di tempat "
"lain."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:111
msgid ""
"The consequence of both corrections is the same: **rebalancing pools cannot "
"help.** Only reducing total job demand can. That is what this change does."
msgstr ""
"Konsekuensi dari kedua koreksi adalah sama: **menyeimbangkan kembali kolam "
"tidak bisa membantu.** Hanya mengurangi total permintaan pekerjaan yang "
"bisa. Itulah perubahan ini."

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:114
msgid "The change"
msgstr "Perubahan"

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:116
msgid ""
"For ten heavy gates, the post-merge arm became a staggered six-hourly sweep "
"plus release tags:"
msgstr ""
"Untuk sepuluh gerbang berat, lengan pasca-merger menjadi penyaringan enam "
"jam bertahap ditambah label rilis:"

#: src/testing/ci-gate-scheduling.md:121
