#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:3
msgid ""
"JavaScript has no `free()`. For most programs that's the right default — "
"Perry's generational GC (see [Memory Model](memory-model.md)) decides when "
"to collect. But latency-sensitive programs (games, interactive UIs) and "
"programs that churn large binary buffers sometimes need to _choose the "
"moment_: run the collection between frames, not in the middle of one; "
"release a 100 MB texture now, not at the next full cycle. Perry gives you "
"two standard-shaped tools for that."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript tidak memiliki `free()`. Untuk sebagian besar program yang "
"merupakan standar yang tepat  Generasi GC Perry (lihat [Model Memori](memory-"
"model.md)) memutuskan kapan untuk mengumpulkan. Tapi program yang sensitif "
"latensi (game, UI interaktif) dan program yang menggulir buffer biner besar "
"kadang-kadang perlu memilih saat: menjalankan koleksi antara bingkai, bukan "
"di tengah satu; melepaskan tekstur 100 MB sekarang, bukan pada siklus penuh "
"berikutnya. Perry memberi Anda dua alat berbentuk standar untuk itu."

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:10
msgid "`ArrayBuffer.prototype.transfer()` (ES2024)"
msgstr "`ArrayBuffer.prototype.transfer()` (ES2024)"

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:12
msgid ""
"`transfer(newLength?)` moves an ArrayBuffer's contents into a new buffer and "
"**detaches** the source: its `byteLength` becomes 0, `detached` reports "
"`true`, views over it report length 0, and any further `transfer`/`slice`/"
"view construction on it throws a `TypeError`. This is standard ECMAScript — "
"the same code runs under Node and Bun unchanged."
msgstr ""
"`transfer(newLength?)` memindahkan isi ArrayBuffer ke buffer baru dan "
"**Pembuangan** sumbernya: `byteLength` menjadi 0, `detached` melaporkan "
"`true`, tampilan di atasnya melaporkan panjang 0, dan setiap konstruksi "
"`transfer` / `slice` / tampilan lebih lanjut di atasnya melemparkan "
"`TypeError`. Ini adalah standar ECMAScript  kode yang sama berjalan di bawah "
"Node dan Bun tidak berubah."

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:18
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"let scratch = new ArrayBuffer(64 * 1024 * 1024);\n"
"// ... use it ...\n"
"scratch = scratch.transfer(0); // detach: the 64 MB backing is released\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"let scratch = new ArrayBuffer(64 * 1024 * 1024);\n"
"// ... use it ...\n"
"scratch = scratch.transfer(0); // detach: the 64 MB backing is released\n"
"```"

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:24
msgid ""
"Perry gives detach real teeth: buffer bytes live inline in the GC heap, so "
"the runtime hands the page-aligned interior of a detached payload back to "
"the OS immediately (`madvise`). A large detached buffer stops costing RSS "
"the moment you transfer it, even while the (now empty) ArrayBuffer object is "
"still reachable. `transferToFixedLength()` behaves identically (Perry has no "
"resizable ArrayBuffers), and `structuredClone(v, { transfer: [...] })` "
"detaches through the same path."
msgstr ""
"Perry memberikan gigi nyata lepas: buffer byte hidup inline di heap GC, "
"sehingga runtime menyerahkan halaman yang diselaraskan interior dari muatan "
"yang lepas kembali ke OS segera (`madvise`). Sebuah buffer terpisah besar "
